from pathlib import Path
import json,html,collections
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((R/'SUMMARY.json').read_text());attempts=json.loads((R/'ATTEMPTS.json').read_text())
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(v))+'</td>' for v in [r['pool'],r['scenario'],str(r['flags'])+'/'+str(r['n']),f"{r['wilson95'][0]:.3f}–{r['wilson95'][1]:.3f}",r['not_estimable'],r['pass_gate']])+'</tr>' for r in s['results'])
doc='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Joint support and feasibility gate</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1050px;margin:40px auto;padding:20px;background:#f8faf7;color:#173c30}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #c5d4c9;text-align:left}table{border-collapse:collapse}</style><h1>Joint gate: '''+s['status']+'''</h1>
<p>Frozen synthetic boundary qualification. Admit only V≥80, at least8supported pages, maximum page share≤.25 and matched available-follower fractions f_ch≥.10,f_sh≥.25. Challenge cases are restricted to80≤V&lt;84. No following-qok outcomes enter selection.</p>
<p>Each positive targets a V-weighted matched rate of.10 after ch and.25 after sh. Adjusted probabilities are used only where qok followers are possible; unavailable followers remain structural zeros. Outcomes are drawn after support/feasibility screening. Nulls use independent probability.2 or.6 on available nonorigin followers and are not prefix-calibrated.</p>
<table><tr><th>Exact bodies</th><th>Scenario</th><th>Flags</th><th>Wilson95</th><th>Not estimable</th><th>Gate</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table>
<p>Each cell requires100 accepted trials. Positive lower power bound must reach.80; null upper false-flag bound must not exceed.10. If the frozen1500-attempt sampling cap cannot supply the quota, that is an incomplete qualification, not a power failure and not permission to extend the cap after seeing results.</p>
<h2>Selection caveat</h2><p>Feasibility depends on prefix orientations and structural follower availability. It need not stay invariant under the conditional null. Therefore the null checks are an essential part of this joint gate; outcome-blind selection alone does not guarantee unbiased inference. Passing these finite controls is not a mathematical proof of validity across arbitrary arrangements.</p>
<p>Within each accepted layout, two nulls and a positive reuse the same matched structure with independently drawn outcomes. They are paired scenarios, not independent replication. Four-body controls are more diverse than one-body controls but remain authored synthetic arrays, not a historical corpus. Exact lengths, variable-length parsing, H/F alignment and actual manuscript support are not qualified by this run.</p>
<p>All rejected support/feasibility cases, sampling failures and outcome failures are preserved. The near-threshold results cannot establish that80 is a universal minimum or that weaker effects are detectable. No Voynich files were read or scored. H/F remain separate.</p>
<p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen rules</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Hashes</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.json">Results</a> · <a href="ATTEMPTS.json">All screened layouts</a> · <a href="TRIALS.json">All outcomes</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a></p>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(doc,encoding='utf-8')
assert all((R/f).exists() for f in ['PROTOCOL.json','FREEZE.json','SUMMARY.json','ATTEMPTS.json','TRIALS.json','VERIFICATION.json'])
